<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's ACCC approves ANI purchase.</title>
<headline>Australia's ACCC approves ANI purchase.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's anti-monopolies regulator said on Tuesday it would not oppose heavy engineer Australian National Industries Ltd's (ANI) purchase of Azon Ltd's National Castings operations.</p>
<p>Azon is an Australian unit of Illinois Tool Works Inc.</p>
<p>The Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) said the acquisition would boost ANI's market share in steel and alloy iron castings, but that its foundries still faced import competition.  </p>
<p>&quot;The ACCC has therefore concluded that the acquisition is unlikely to substantially lessen competition,&quot; ACCC chairman Alan Fels said in a statement.</p>
<p>ANI bought National Castings Pty Ltd for A$21.5 million.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
